                "title":"Getting an Endoscopy",
                "line1":"This social story was developed by Dr. Mojdeh Mostafavi, a pediatric fellow in gastroenterology at Mass General Hospital for Children. Learn more by visiting https://www.massgeneral.org/children/gastroenterology.<br>This story is about how I can get an endoscopy. If I feel nervous, I can<ul><li>Think of something that makes me happy</li><li>Ask someone to hold my hand</li><li>Use calming exercises like counting</li></ul>",
                "line2":"To get ready for my test, I will need to have a special drink. The drink will help me poop. My belly might feel different, but it will not hurt.",
                "line3":"In the morning, I am going to wake up, but I am not going to eat or drink. I will still be able to have medicine.",
                "line4":"Then I will go to the hospital, check in, and wait until the nurses are ready to help me get ready in the examination room.",
                "line5":"The nurse in the room will check my weight, and after that I will take off all my clothes. They will give me a hospital gown to wear, and I may feel cold. If I am cold, I can use a warm blanket.",
                "line6":"Then the nurse will check my temperature. They may touch my face or arm with the thermometer, but it will not hurt. If I am nervous or uncomfortable, I can count to 20.",
                "line7":"The nurse will check my blood pressure after taking my temperature. They will wrap a band around my arm that will give me a big squeeze. It will not hurt. If I am nervous or uncomfortable, I can count to 20.",
                "line8":"The nurse will check my oxygen after by putting a clip on my finger that shines a red light. It will not hurt. If I am nervous or uncomfortable, I can count to 20.",
                "line9":"While I’m waiting, it is okay to feel nervous or scared. I will remind myself that I am safe and that there are nurses, doctors, and a child life specialist to all help take care of me. They will answer my questions, and the doctor may give me medicine to help me relax.",
                "line10":"To get ready for my test, I may go under anesthesia with an IV. For this, I will get an IV, which is a special straw that goes in my hand or arm. The doctor can give me special water and medicine through my IV. I am safe while using an IV.",
                "line11":"The nurse will push on my hand or arm. They will wrap a rubber band around my arm- it will feel tight. Then the nurse will clean my arm with a swab- this will feel cold and wet.",
                "line12":"The nurse will put the special straw in my arm using a needle. This will feel like a poke or sting, and it may hurt a little bit. If I am nervous or uncomfortable, I can count to 20. When this is done, the nurse will take the needle away.",
                "line13":"The nurse will put tape on the special tube. I will see blood coming out of my body, but my body will make more blood. I am safe.",
                "line14":"The nurse will connect the IV to special water or medicine. This will make me feel better! I will not touch or pull on my IV.",
